Overlay patch 0062 (DECISIONS D13 = Shipwright D-085 + D-087, overlays 0066
+ 0068): SPIKE ATTRIBUTION PROBE + MENU-PHASE SPLIT. Instrument only -- no
behaviour change. Default ON (gSohIos.SpikeProbe = 1, polled every 60 frames).

WHAT IT MEASURES (formats identical to Shipwright's, so one reader parses
every port). Every 2D frame is cut at overlay 0061's pace seams (drawable
acquired / LUS sleep begins) plus three marks inside
Fast3dWindow::DrawAndRunGraphicsCommands, and the record closes right after
Interpreter::EndFrame:
  gap    previous frame's end -> this frame's drawable request: the game
         frame's logic on the first frame of each game frame (logic), the
         audio hand-off wait (aud), SDL_PumpEvents = every UIKit main-thread
         callback (ev), FrameInterpolation_Interpolate (interp).
  wait   nextDrawable.
  busy   drawable -> LUS sleep, split into menu (ImGui NewFrame + DrawMenu +
         CalculateGameViewport), run (StartFrame + display list), gui
         (EndDraw), end (Interpreter::EndFrame: commit + present).
  cpu    gap + busy; a frame whose cpu exceeds 1000 / interpolation fps is a
         SPIKE.
Seam categories: res (resource cache miss loaded on the game thread, n/ms/
bytes + the 3 largest by name), bg (misses loaded on pool threads), rwait
(LoadResource on the game thread), tex (ImportTexture), shd
(CreateAndLoadNewShader), fbrd (ReadFramebufferToCPU), cvsave (CVar saves),
aud (push_frame's audio wait), ev (wnd->HandleEvents: the SDL pump), interp,
plus tris/vtx/draws per frame. (rd/up/zdep/zpso/actor/obj/room keep their
Shipwright slots but are not wired on MK64 -- see SohIosSpike.cpp.)
MENU SPLIT: ten marks P..I through Gui::StartDraw (this LUS fork has no
Fast3dGui: P/A/B/H/I live in LUS Gui.cpp, C..G in SpaghettiGui::DrawMenu,
which overrides Gui::DrawMenu) with wall + thread-CPU time per
sub-bucket and every GuiWindow timed by name: SOH_MSLOW per >= 4 ms menu
phase, SOH_MENUWIN per 10 s. This is the instrument that found Shipwright's
D-087 (LUS's SDLAddRemoveDeviceEventHandler pumps SDL -- and with it the
touch overlay's full-screen Core Graphics repaints -- inside DrawMenu).

Files: creates src/port/SohIosSpike.cpp (source of truth:
overlay/assets/SohIosSpike.cpp), seams in Fast3dWindow.cpp, interpreter.cpp,
gfx_metal.cpp, ResourceManager.cpp (after overlay 0029's timing block, reusing
its start time), Gui.cpp, consolevariablebridge.cpp, FrameInterpolation.cpp
and Engine.cpp (EndAudioFrame). Every hunk keeps clear of earlier patches'
hunks and their 3-line contexts.

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0061 applied and 0062 not applied.


